/* The Outliner, as Blender's Outliner and Unity's Hierarchy: the scene as a
   root row with its object count, then a row per object the object filter
   shows, in a List the host windows (data-list-rows) and whose rows the
   Outliner's behaviors fill as self.rows (OutlinerRows, over the editor
   nodes of studio_nodes.c). A row selects on click, with Mod and Shift
   for several; double-click or F2 renames it in place; its eye and lock show
   while it is hovered or while they are on; it takes behaviors and the
   assets its fields name, and the list takes prototypes. The list is one
   Tab stop, and while the keyboard holds it the active row shows the focus
   ring and Studio's keys act on it. */
body { overflow: hidden; padding: 0dp; }
.outliner-panel { position: absolute; left: 0dp; top: 0dp; right: 0dp; bottom: 0dp; }
.list {
  position: absolute; left: 0dp; top: 0dp; right: 0dp; bottom: 0dp; height: auto; padding: 3dp 4dp 8dp;
  tab-index: auto;
}
.outliner-row { display: block; }
/* The eye and lock take the row's whole height, so a press anywhere in
   their column toggles instead of selecting the row. */
.tree-row .trail, .view-toggles { align-self: stretch; }
.view-toggles .toggle { align-self: stretch; height: auto; tab-index: none; }
.list:focus-visible .tree-row[data-active] { border-color: var(--ring); }
/* The name's field starts where a row's icon does, past the twisty's room. */
.object-rename { padding-left: 38dp; }
